  "about": "NativeDeckCanonicalNames.candidates (Archidekt link imports, 2026-10-26): the names a deck's card is looked up by, in order. The exact name first; then plain letters for accents (XMage spells names without them); then a spelling alias for the three XMage 1.4.63 ellipsis renames; then the front of a two-part name (adventure, omen and prepare cards, whose full name only Archidekt sends). A tight ellipsis that is still the catalogue name (More of That Strange Oil...) is not folded. Double-faced cards keep their aliases, and an exact split-card name always wins because it comes first.",
